---
name: write-prd
description: Write or refine a feature spec (prd.md and acceptance.json) for a change to this existing code base. Use before any code for a new feature or behaviour change.
---

# Write a PRD

1. `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc new <slug>` creates `.ai/specs/FEAT-<nnn>-<slug>/` from the template (or `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc spec <document>` drafts it from a requirements document).
2. Read `.ai/rules/prd.md` for the structure. Read the code the change touches first: the spec must describe the behaviour that exists today and what changes.
3. Write the acceptance criteria: observable, one behaviour each, with unhappy paths and boundaries. Add every existing behaviour the change must not break under "Existing behaviour that must keep working".
4. Write `acceptance.json` (skill: write-fact-checks). Every criterion needs a check; every check cites a criterion.
5. Remove every `TODO(prd)` marker. `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc facts --feature FEAT-<nnn>` must report the traceability as PASS.
6. A human reviews the spec (skill: review-spec) before `implement`.

Do not invent requirements. Anything you had to assume goes in the last section as a line starting with `ASSUMPTION:`.
